1
00:00:00,493 --> 00:00:04,493
[bright music]

2
00:00:47,250 --> 00:00:48,666
So how have you been?

3
00:00:48,708 --> 00:00:50,583
You know, I tried to reach out
to you for a couple of months.

4
00:00:50,625 --> 00:00:52,999
But you weren’t responding.
You weren’t answering my calls.

5
00:00:53,041 --> 00:00:54,250
Yeah, same here.

6
00:00:54,458 --> 00:00:56,125
Yeah, um…

7
00:00:57,750 --> 00:01:00,791
I’m sorry about that. I just, um...

8
00:01:02,125 --> 00:01:05,375
It was... It was really
hard after the breakup.

9
00:01:06,666 --> 00:01:09,374
It’s alright. It’s been over a year.

10
00:01:09,416 --> 00:01:11,458
Have you reached out to Ivan and Dave?

11
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:16,999
Alright, I understand.

12
00:01:17,041 --> 00:01:21,000
Let’s not talk about them.
And let’s talk about you.

13
00:01:21,166 --> 00:01:23,291
I know you have something to tell us.

14
00:01:23,458 --> 00:01:25,499
First, do you need anything?

15
00:01:25,541 --> 00:01:28,791
Cause I’d be more than
happy to help. Just let me know.

16
00:01:30,750 --> 00:01:32,958
Well, I’m seeing someone right now.

17
00:01:35,833 --> 00:01:37,958
- Alright. - Okay.

18
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,416
That’s... good. Who is he?

19
00:01:47,250 --> 00:01:49,333
He’s my roommate.

20
00:01:52,916 --> 00:01:54,708
Yeah, um...

21
00:01:55,625 --> 00:01:58,833
We’ve been living together
for a few weeks now.

22
00:01:59,791 --> 00:02:01,208
Oh, Interesting.

23
00:02:01,250 --> 00:02:03,958
Wow, yeah. Tell us… Tell us more.

24
00:02:04,250 --> 00:02:05,458
Well...

25
00:02:06,375 --> 00:02:08,791
he just proposed.

26
00:02:12,041 --> 00:02:13,416
Over...

27
00:02:13,458 --> 00:02:15,875
coffee and bread and hotdogs.

28
00:02:18,958 --> 00:02:19,916
I'm...

29
00:02:19,958 --> 00:02:22,791
- I’m so sorry. I didn’t mean to make…
- No, no. It's... It's okay.

30
00:02:22,833 --> 00:02:26,416
I... I think about it, too.
And I can’t help but...

31
00:02:30,375 --> 00:02:32,875
Wait, what are you gonna do?

32
00:02:36,272 --> 00:02:38,749
[soft music]

33
00:02:38,791 --> 00:02:40,250
I don’t know.

34
00:02:44,750 --> 00:02:46,124
Do you...

35
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:47,833
Do you like him?

36
00:02:48,708 --> 00:02:49,708
Uh,

37
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,750
I guess so, yeah.

38
00:02:54,458 --> 00:02:57,124
Guess? But do you like him enough to...

39
00:02:57,166 --> 00:02:58,541
you know.

40
00:03:03,750 --> 00:03:06,458
I’m not even sure if I’m ready for-

41
00:03:15,041 --> 00:03:17,708
Honey, no, no, no…

42
00:03:17,750 --> 00:03:20,041
Hey, it’s okay. Don’t cry.

43
00:03:20,291 --> 00:03:22,124
Listen, you’ve been through a lot.

44
00:03:22,166 --> 00:03:25,208
You... You deserve to be happy.

45
00:03:25,791 --> 00:03:29,750
What I’m about to say is just
based on my personal experience.

46
00:03:30,333 --> 00:03:33,875
You know we love you.
And you know we’re for you.

47
00:03:34,250 --> 00:03:38,000
Even though you chose to stay away
from us after your breakup with Ivan.

48
00:03:38,333 --> 00:03:43,375
I think, before you make
any other major life decisions,

49
00:03:43,625 --> 00:03:45,249
you need to let go.

50
00:03:45,291 --> 00:03:47,375
You need to learn how to let go.

51
00:03:49,625 --> 00:03:52,208
You need to forgive Ivan.

52
00:03:55,541 --> 00:03:57,583
And most importantly,

53
00:03:58,166 --> 00:04:00,916
you need to forgive yourself.

54
00:04:02,458 --> 00:04:05,416
You just loved someone too much.

55
00:04:13,150 --> 00:04:17,150
[dramatic music]

56
00:05:15,541 --> 00:05:17,374
Hey, where have you been?

57
00:05:17,416 --> 00:05:19,208
I’ve been waiting for you.

58
00:05:21,125 --> 00:05:23,666
And listen, about what
I said earlier, just...

59
00:05:23,708 --> 00:05:24,791
forget about it.

60
00:05:24,833 --> 00:05:26,916
I was being stupid and -

61
00:05:26,958 --> 00:05:28,708
You should go home.

62
00:05:30,583 --> 00:05:31,750
What?

63
00:05:32,791 --> 00:05:35,458
You should go back to the Philippines.

64
00:05:36,791 --> 00:05:39,791
You’re drunk. And you don’t
know what you’re saying.

65
00:05:39,833 --> 00:05:41,583
Let’s talk about this tomorrow.

66
00:05:41,625 --> 00:05:43,416
You’re tired. You need some rest.

67
00:05:43,666 --> 00:05:46,666
No. I... I know what I’m saying just fine.

68
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,416
And I want you to fucking leave.

69
00:05:53,125 --> 00:05:55,499
This is about the proposal, right?

70
00:05:55,541 --> 00:05:59,041
Don’t worry about it. I spoke
to the immigration lawyer.

71
00:05:59,083 --> 00:06:00,791
And I have other options.

72
00:06:00,833 --> 00:06:02,791
I don’t care what the fucking lawyer said.

73
00:06:02,833 --> 00:06:04,041
I want you to go home.

74
00:06:04,083 --> 00:06:06,874
I want you to go back to Manila.
I’ll book the flight if I have to.

75
00:06:06,916 --> 00:06:08,749
I’ll do it myself.

76
00:06:08,791 --> 00:06:10,250
Just get out.

77
00:06:12,333 --> 00:06:13,833
Joshua, please.

78
00:06:14,458 --> 00:06:16,083
- Joshua, please. - No, no.

79
00:06:16,125 --> 00:06:17,458
Joshua...

80
00:06:18,291 --> 00:06:20,666
I shouldn’t have done what I did.

81
00:06:21,208 --> 00:06:25,041
- I’m sorry and I just - - Let me go.

82
00:06:25,750 --> 00:06:28,874
Promise I won’t do
anything that stupid again.

83
00:06:28,916 --> 00:06:30,041
Please.

84
00:06:30,875 --> 00:06:32,583
Don’t make me leave.

85
00:06:34,595 --> 00:06:36,749
[soft music]

86
00:06:36,791 --> 00:06:38,708
Why do you want to stay?

87
00:06:49,833 --> 00:06:53,250
You can’t even tell me
why you want to stay.

88
00:06:55,833 --> 00:06:58,291
Because I want to be with you!

89
00:06:58,416 --> 00:06:59,750
Fuck you!

90
00:07:00,125 --> 00:07:02,000
You barely know me.

91
00:07:04,208 --> 00:07:06,124
You have a great life
back in the Philippines.

92
00:07:06,166 --> 00:07:08,499
You’re... You're making
films. You’re winning awards.

93
00:07:08,541 --> 00:07:11,625
And you want to throw all of
that away just to be with me?

94
00:07:11,958 --> 00:07:13,958
And… And your Mom.

95
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:17,791
She did other people’s laundry when you
were growing up just to make ends meet.

96
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,499
And now, she’s out in the Middle East,

97
00:07:20,541 --> 00:07:22,291
God only knows if she’s safe.

98
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:26,833
Just to support you and whatever
you want to do with your fucking life.

99
00:07:26,875 --> 00:07:28,458
And you want to throw...

100
00:07:28,583 --> 00:07:31,083
You want to throw away
all her years of sacrifice

101
00:07:31,125 --> 00:07:34,500
just to be with some guy
you’ve only known a few weeks?

102
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:39,541
Because that’s for her. For my dreams.

103
00:07:40,125 --> 00:07:41,958
Well, you can’t work here.

104
00:07:42,693 --> 00:07:45,458
[soft music]

105
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:48,166
Which is why I asked you to marry me.

106
00:07:49,250 --> 00:07:51,416
Well, I can’t marry you.

107
00:07:52,666 --> 00:07:53,333
Why?

108
00:07:53,375 --> 00:07:55,625
Because I’m already married!

109
00:08:00,291 --> 00:08:02,624
I was young and stupid.

110
00:08:02,666 --> 00:08:06,666
And I was only thinking
about how I felt about him.

111
00:08:07,541 --> 00:08:10,541
He was… He was also a visitor like you.

112
00:08:10,791 --> 00:08:14,166
And he was also afraid of overstaying.

113
00:08:14,375 --> 00:08:18,416
And he said he couldn’t achieve
his dreams if he was illegal.

114
00:08:18,458 --> 00:08:21,041
And so I was over here, uh,

115
00:08:21,083 --> 00:08:22,958
trying to be a hero.

116
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,041
Trying to be a savior.

117
00:08:26,083 --> 00:08:28,375
And I agreed to marry him.

118
00:08:28,583 --> 00:08:31,333
I thought if I give him what he needed,

119
00:08:31,875 --> 00:08:36,500
that everything would be fine and
we would be happy together forever.

120
00:08:36,833 --> 00:08:40,833
But a few months after our wedding,

121
00:08:41,916 --> 00:08:44,166
I found out he’s cheating on me.

122
00:08:44,875 --> 00:08:47,708
Do you know how badly I
wanted to get back at him?

123
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,624
How... How badly I
wanted to make him suffer.

124
00:08:50,666 --> 00:08:53,625
To make him feel the way he made me feel.

125
00:08:53,791 --> 00:08:55,583
And it would be so easy.

126
00:08:55,625 --> 00:08:58,916
All I have to do, right
now, is file for divorce.

127
00:08:58,958 --> 00:09:00,541
Because then, he
couldn’t get his green card.

128
00:09:00,583 --> 00:09:03,750
He needs to be married to me for two years.

129
00:09:04,958 --> 00:09:07,750
And he couldn’t even stay with me for one.

130
00:09:09,041 --> 00:09:10,416
Fucking idiot.

131
00:09:10,791 --> 00:09:14,750
Left me for someone with a lot more money.

132
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:20,875
It’s just like I said, it’s always
just been about the money!

133
00:09:22,583 --> 00:09:24,750
And you know what the most painful part is?

134
00:09:25,166 --> 00:09:26,833
I still

135
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:29,458
care about him.

136
00:09:30,625 --> 00:09:35,416
And I hate that I care so much
about him after what he did to me.

137
00:09:36,208 --> 00:09:37,375
But I do.

138
00:09:39,583 --> 00:09:42,208
I think about him all the fucking time.

139
00:09:42,791 --> 00:09:45,291
I'm thinking about how he’s doing.

140
00:09:45,333 --> 00:09:48,000
Is he okay? Is he happy?

141
00:09:49,208 --> 00:09:51,041
Is all the money worth it?

142
00:09:55,125 --> 00:09:57,125
And I’m sorry, but

143
00:09:57,458 --> 00:09:59,208
you deserve to know this.

144
00:10:05,458 --> 00:10:07,750
I still think about him

145
00:10:08,791 --> 00:10:11,000
even when I’m with you.

146
00:11:00,204 --> 00:11:04,204
[crying]

147
00:11:41,409 --> 00:11:45,409
[dramatic music]

148
00:13:12,348 --> 00:13:16,348
[soft music]

149
00:13:28,125 --> 00:13:29,791
Bestfriend, get up.

150
00:13:34,666 --> 00:13:36,833
What are you doing here?

151
00:13:38,958 --> 00:13:41,208
Don't start with me! Get up!

152
00:13:51,833 --> 00:13:53,708
What's the matter with you?

153
00:13:54,458 --> 00:13:56,833
Nothing. But you, you've
got a lot of problems!

154
00:13:57,041 --> 00:13:58,583
Leave me alone!

155
00:13:59,750 --> 00:14:01,875
Be grateful, you're handsome or else

156
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,541
I would've punched you in the face!

157
00:14:03,583 --> 00:14:05,166
Your so annoying!

158
00:14:13,250 --> 00:14:15,166
Your mom keeps on calling me.

159
00:14:16,541 --> 00:14:18,500
She's worried sick.

160
00:14:19,625 --> 00:14:21,333
You're not responding to her.

161
00:14:22,250 --> 00:14:25,083
I just told her that you're busy
with the script you're working on.

162
00:14:28,833 --> 00:14:31,000
Who told you to do that?

163
00:14:31,958 --> 00:14:33,833
Why don't you all go to hell? F♪ck you all!

164
00:14:34,833 --> 00:14:36,250
Fuck you, too!

165
00:14:37,333 --> 00:14:38,333
Damn you!

166
00:14:38,875 --> 00:14:40,833
You're just going to end up like that?

167
00:14:42,250 --> 00:14:44,208
Wasted all the time?

168
00:14:45,541 --> 00:14:47,416
Well, you're not a kid anymore, Andre.

169
00:14:48,291 --> 00:14:51,458
You're wasting a lot of opportunities!

170
00:14:52,208 --> 00:14:56,000
Stop blaming that f♪ucking love

171
00:14:56,250 --> 00:14:58,041
for why your life's so wasted!

172
00:14:58,291 --> 00:15:00,291
You've only got yourself to blame!

173
00:15:01,833 --> 00:15:05,166
And only you can help
yourself, no one else!

174
00:15:14,065 --> 00:15:18,065
[crying]

175
00:15:40,458 --> 00:15:41,916
I can't forget him.

176
00:16:00,041 --> 00:16:03,083
That moment when I left him

177
00:16:04,458 --> 00:16:06,333
knowing how miserable he was.

178
00:16:09,125 --> 00:16:10,500
I wonder how he's doing now.

179
00:16:13,375 --> 00:16:14,541
The memories of him

180
00:16:14,583 --> 00:16:15,250
The memories of him

181
00:16:16,833 --> 00:16:18,250
keep on haunting me.

182
00:16:20,541 --> 00:16:21,958
Bestfriend,

183
00:16:24,125 --> 00:16:26,750
if you're really worried about him,

184
00:16:28,958 --> 00:16:31,583
it's best to work on yourself first.

185
00:16:34,083 --> 00:16:38,541
How can you help him if
you can't even help yourself?

186
00:16:41,632 --> 00:16:44,083
[soft music]

187
00:16:44,125 --> 00:16:45,500
If I were you,

188
00:16:46,833 --> 00:16:48,791
I'd finish your film project.

189
00:16:49,250 --> 00:16:51,708
Attend another film festival in America.

190
00:16:52,416 --> 00:16:54,291
So you could see and visit him again.

191
00:16:56,500 --> 00:16:57,916
But if you're wasted all the time,

192
00:16:58,041 --> 00:17:00,000
nothing will happen.

193
00:17:01,958 --> 00:17:06,125
Life has to continue moving
forward even if you're lonely.

194
00:17:08,500 --> 00:17:10,208
F♪ck that scammer!

195
00:17:12,833 --> 00:17:14,750
I shouldn't have met Joshua.

196
00:17:17,166 --> 00:17:19,041
Why don't you write to him?

197
00:17:19,375 --> 00:17:20,916
Email him.

198
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,875
Curse him all you want.

199
00:17:25,666 --> 00:17:28,666
Let him know how you feel.

200
00:17:30,166 --> 00:17:31,833
Believe me, bestfriend,

201
00:17:32,041 --> 00:17:33,875
it's very effective.

202
00:17:35,333 --> 00:17:38,166
Of all the things I've been through,

203
00:17:40,375 --> 00:17:43,625
it's the most effective way to let go.

204
00:17:44,853 --> 00:17:48,853
[soft music]

205
00:17:51,541 --> 00:17:54,125
And I always remind you, bestfriend,

206
00:17:55,083 --> 00:17:57,458
just because you love someone

207
00:17:58,458 --> 00:18:00,874
doesn't mean they'll love you in return.

208
00:18:00,916 --> 00:18:02,958
Life’s not like that.

209
00:18:22,056 --> 00:18:26,056
[soft music]

210
00:18:46,416 --> 00:18:47,833
Hi Joshua,

211
00:18:48,833 --> 00:18:52,333
I am writing this email
because I want to say

212
00:18:54,750 --> 00:18:56,666
fuck you!

213
00:18:58,666 --> 00:19:01,041
I didn’t deserve what you did to me!

214
00:19:01,958 --> 00:19:05,041
Being hurt doesn’t give you
the right to hurt other people!

215
00:19:07,666 --> 00:19:09,541
I have nothing to do with your past!

216
00:19:09,583 --> 00:19:11,875
I am not the one who cheated on you!

217
00:19:13,875 --> 00:19:18,250
And if I were, I’d stop blaming
other people for your own misery.

218
00:19:46,916 --> 00:19:48,625
Hi, Joshua.

219
00:19:50,333 --> 00:19:52,083
I hope you’re okay.

220
00:19:55,083 --> 00:19:58,416
I know we were not able to
properly say goodbye to each other.

221
00:20:01,208 --> 00:20:03,708
And I’m sorry for that.

222
00:20:05,541 --> 00:20:09,833
I chose to leave before I had
the chance to fully understand

223
00:20:10,125 --> 00:20:12,083
what you’ve been going through.

224
00:20:16,411 --> 00:20:20,411
[soft music]

225
00:20:25,250 --> 00:20:27,583
I chose to get mad at you

226
00:20:27,708 --> 00:20:31,000
when what you really needed
was a shoulder to cry on.

227
00:20:33,083 --> 00:20:37,958
I haven’t even thanked you for
all the things you’ve done for me.

228
00:20:39,875 --> 00:20:42,416
When I was looking for a place to stay,

229
00:20:43,500 --> 00:20:45,500
you let me into yours.

230
00:20:46,958 --> 00:20:49,333
You chose to help me many times,

231
00:20:49,791 --> 00:20:52,750
even when you were the one who needed help.

232
00:20:54,458 --> 00:20:58,083
You were suffering, bleeding on the inside,

233
00:20:58,125 --> 00:21:01,750
but you never cried for help.

234
00:21:02,875 --> 00:21:05,791
You seemed so strong,

235
00:21:05,833 --> 00:21:07,958
I didn’t realize

236
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,625
that worse things were happening to you.

237
00:21:12,041 --> 00:21:16,416
You chose to love me at a time when

238
00:21:17,291 --> 00:21:20,000
you didn’t have that much love to give.

239
00:21:20,958 --> 00:21:23,458
You were right about one thing,

240
00:21:24,041 --> 00:21:26,541
I’ve been selfish.

241
00:21:33,750 --> 00:21:37,833
I didn’t realize how lucky I am.

242
00:21:41,916 --> 00:21:46,041
Because there are people in my
life who keep on cheering for me

243
00:21:46,791 --> 00:21:48,958
no matter how much I screw up.

244
00:21:52,125 --> 00:21:53,541
Listen, you’ve been through a lot.

245
00:21:56,513 --> 00:22:00,513
[soft music]

246
00:22:01,375 --> 00:22:03,875
And I will forever regret

247
00:22:04,208 --> 00:22:06,291
not staying behind

248
00:22:06,750 --> 00:22:09,208
when you needed me the most.

249
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:40,083
I really missed you, Joshua.

250
00:22:42,166 --> 00:22:44,541
I hope I get to see you again.

251
00:22:45,500 --> 00:22:46,583
And

252
00:22:46,875 --> 00:22:49,291
I’m going to do my best
to make that happen.

253
00:22:49,791 --> 00:22:53,208
I just hope that when the time comes,

254
00:22:53,416 --> 00:22:55,958
I’m a little more mature

255
00:22:56,000 --> 00:23:00,291
and maybe can give you
what you actually deserve.

256
00:23:01,958 --> 00:23:03,208
For now,

257
00:23:03,250 --> 00:23:06,625
I’m just gonna think of
our memories together.

258
00:23:08,375 --> 00:23:11,500
And I don’t know if this helps

259
00:23:11,916 --> 00:23:13,000
but

260
00:23:13,625 --> 00:23:15,749
just know that someone,

261
00:23:15,791 --> 00:23:17,416
thousands of miles away,

262
00:23:17,875 --> 00:23:19,791
still cares about you.

263
00:23:29,404 --> 00:23:33,404
[dramatic music]

264
00:24:28,478 --> 00:24:32,478
[dramatic music]

265
00:24:39,625 --> 00:24:41,000
Hello?

266
00:24:41,375 --> 00:24:44,875
Who’s this? Don't... Don’t you
know it’s two in the morning?

267
00:24:46,250 --> 00:24:47,541
Oh.

268
00:24:49,166 --> 00:24:50,875
Hi, Josh...

269
00:24:52,333 --> 00:24:53,500
ua.

270
00:25:29,500 --> 00:25:30,541
Where are you going?

271
00:25:30,583 --> 00:25:33,791
And don’t tell me work?
It’s already ten at night.

272
00:25:33,833 --> 00:25:36,125
No, I’m meeting Bob and Wayne.

273
00:25:36,625 --> 00:25:38,166
Mm... Good!

274
00:25:39,208 --> 00:25:40,833
And where are you guys headed to?

275
00:25:41,208 --> 00:25:41,833
Ahh...

276
00:25:41,875 --> 00:25:43,625
Some bar in We-Ho.

277
00:25:43,875 --> 00:25:45,166
Oh, so you’re…

278
00:25:45,208 --> 00:25:47,041
you’re gonna be partying in We-Ho?

279
00:25:47,500 --> 00:25:49,333
Is there something wrong with that?

280
00:25:49,375 --> 00:25:50,541
No, uh...

281
00:25:50,583 --> 00:25:52,124
why would there be?

282
00:25:52,166 --> 00:25:55,500
You should go out as much as you like.

283
00:25:55,708 --> 00:25:56,791
I just…

284
00:25:57,083 --> 00:25:58,791
I just wish I could join you guys.

285
00:25:58,833 --> 00:25:59,750
Ahh...

286
00:26:00,541 --> 00:26:02,166
So when are you coming?

287
00:26:05,166 --> 00:26:06,125
What?

288
00:26:06,333 --> 00:26:07,708
Uh, well,

289
00:26:08,041 --> 00:26:11,125
actually, I have some good news for you.

290
00:26:11,291 --> 00:26:12,166
Okay.

291
00:26:12,291 --> 00:26:14,666
Just make sure it’s really a good news.

292
00:26:16,250 --> 00:26:16,958
It is.

293
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:17,791
Uh,

294
00:26:17,916 --> 00:26:19,874
My first feature film,

295
00:26:19,916 --> 00:26:23,541
the project I’ve been working
on for the past year and a half,

296
00:26:24,625 --> 00:26:27,458
it’s officially been accepted
into a festival in New York.

297
00:26:27,791 --> 00:26:29,125
Okay, uh...

298
00:26:30,291 --> 00:26:31,291
Well,

299
00:26:32,916 --> 00:26:34,708
New York is far.

300
00:26:36,333 --> 00:26:37,666
Oh, really?

301
00:26:37,791 --> 00:26:39,166
Yeah, I mean, it’s…

302
00:26:39,291 --> 00:26:41,000
it’s on the other coast.

303
00:26:42,666 --> 00:26:44,124
I have to go soon. But just

304
00:26:44,166 --> 00:26:45,958
tell me when the
festival’s going to happen,

305
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:47,500
So I can take a leave.

306
00:26:48,291 --> 00:26:50,416
Uh, one week, two weeks,

307
00:26:50,458 --> 00:26:51,416
I don’t care.

308
00:26:51,583 --> 00:26:52,708
I’ll be there.

309
00:26:53,458 --> 00:26:54,625
Bye.

310
00:26:55,000 --> 00:26:57,208
Oh wait, wait, before you go…

311
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:02,666
Well,

312
00:27:03,166 --> 00:27:04,250
bye Josh...

313
00:27:04,875 --> 00:27:05,583
ua.

314
00:27:17,196 --> 00:27:21,196
[dramatic music]
